### S5. Stored derivations recompute exactly (LOW, role task C)

From stored `pooled_f32` (numpy float64 formula; fp32-torch exactness needs a model rerun — see section 4):

- int8 `clip(round(127*tanh))`: 0/677,888 mismatches (0.000000%).
- packed `packbits(pooled>=0)`: 0/84,736 mismatches.
- hashes vs `data/RT01.json` texts: 662/662 match.
- `tokenizer_stats.json` vs all 20 `*_untrunc_len.npy`: 20/20 match on (n, max, mean, trunc_gt1024); all trunc counts 0, all empty counts 0.
- Reference formulas confirmed against `official_st_quantize.py` (Int8TanhQuantizer: round(tanh*127) clamp; BinaryTanhQuantizer: where(x>=0,1,-1); PackedBinaryQuantizer: packbits(x>=0)).
- 15 checkpoints cover 120 unique rows; orphaned slow-run leftovers, superseded by the fast-run payload (615 rows, mtime Sep 16 14:21 vs checkpoints Sep 15 16:35–37).

### S6. "4.3 texts/s (73 tok/s)" unsourced (LOW)

`FINDINGS_DIGEST.md:124` attributes ~4.3 texts/s to the abandoned encoder. Observed: `progress.json` 0.064 texts/s (first cold batch), `progress_fast.json` 1.82 texts/s, `encode.log` no throughput lines, no diag output logs exist. No artifact shows 4.3 or 73 tok/s → UNVERIFIED figure. The ABANDONED conclusion itself is supported (S1–S2), so this dents a parenthetical, not a verdict. Not CRITICAL.

### S7. Leakage question (LOW, role task E)

- Encoder: pretrained PPLX weights, inference only (`inference_mode`, `model.eval`). Nothing fitted on eval data. No leak.
- Scorers/ranking/metrics take no gold/qid params (signature test covers).
- PCA96 (`score_pplx.py:56-63`): fit on concatenated RealTalk DOCUMENT INT8 across all 10 archives — transductive in the same sense as the round-2 main-pipeline finding — BUT: (a) declared in PROTOCOL.md:9 and the module docstring ("fit on REALTALK DOCUMENT INT8 ONLY … no query/gold fit"), (b) queries projected with the saved doc mean, (c) NEVER EXECUTED (S2). No hidden fitting; no quiet transductive number in any report. Forward caution only: if ever run, an inductive (held-out) PCA arm should accompany it per the round-2 lesson.

### S8. Fidelity fix landed before the surviving payload (LOW)

Diff `semantic_before_fidelity_fix/` vs `semantic/`:

- `pplx_scorer.py`: int8/pool float64-numpy → torch-fp32 (matches official ST CPU FP32); added fail-closed `load_checkpoint` (old encoder marked `have[:]=True` on any hash match — would finalize zero rows as complete).
- `encode_pplx.py`: adopts `load_checkpoint`. `score_pplx.py`: adds complete/finite/hash gates.
- Mtimes: fix files Sep 15 16:26–27, GREEN log Sep 15 16:28, surviving payload Sep 16 14:21 via fast writer → payload postdates the fix. On this payload the fix is immaterial anyway: pooled |x| ≤ 1.04, int8 boundary-hit rate 0 (S5). The old resume bug never fired here (hashes 662/662, missings honestly flagged). No stale-fidelity finding.

## (4) What could NOT be checked and why

- Pooling fp32-exactness on real hidden states: needs the 2.4 GB model + hours of CPU encode; each probe kept <15 min per instructions, so no model run attempted. Mitigated by S5 (downstream int8/packed exact on stored poolings).
- Counterfactual semantic scores (would PPLX contradict STOP?): unknowable — embeddings for 9.5 archives + all queries do not exist. Not a gap in this audit; it is why the line was abandoned.
- `_wt_top10/*/semantic/` mirror: listed only (same filenames observed), not diffed — out of role scope, sources read-only regardless.
- `diag_speed.py` / `diag_mask.py`: never run (no logs); slowness cause genuinely undiagnosed, consistent with digest wording.
- Model provenance (MODEL_DOWNLOAD.json / weight_headers.txt / remote-code review claims in `encode_pplx.py:7-13`): not re-verified; no retrieval claim depends on them.
- "1970 unaudited files" beyond semantic/: not my role; I name only what I opened (section A + S3 grep list).

